1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[theme music playing]

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
[Johness] I’ll tear your body apart.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Huh?

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
[heart beating]

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[groans]

17
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
LAST TEST X OF X RESOLVE

18
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
[narrator]
The Exam’s Third Phase required applicants

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
to reach Trick Tower’s base
within 72 hours.

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
But Gon and his friends incurred a penalty

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
and were forced to wait for 50 hours.

22
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Meanwhile...

23
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[rumble]

24
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[announcer] Geretta, applicant 384,
is the fourth to pass.

25
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Time elapsed, 12 hours and 27 minutes.

26
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Well not bad, I guess.

27
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[board click-clacks]

28
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Be careful not to hesitate
on the first step

29
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
or you’re gonna hurt yourself.

30
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
-Here.
-I gotcha.

31
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Hey, Kurapika.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Once we’ve finished
spending our 50 hours here,

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
we’ll have
less than ten hours left, right?

34
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Yes. That’s correct.

35
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Great! [laughs] That’s way more time
than we’ll need, so no harm done!

36
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
-You’re a fool.
-What’s that?

37
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
The Third Phase of the Hunter Exam
is supposed to take 72 hours.

38
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
And each new phase weeds out
more of the applicants

39
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
cutting the field roughly in half
every time.

40
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
In other words, it’s meant
to take 72 hours on average.

41
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
The fact you didn’t know that is proof
that you’re an idiot.

42
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[annoyed grumble]

43
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Then, our chances
of reaching the finish within ten hours

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
will depend on the remaining trials.

45
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Yeah. I guess you’ve got a point.

46
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Hm. It’s too bad you’re so unlucky

47
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
you can’t even win a game
of rock paper scissors when it counts.

48
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
What’d you say?!

49
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
You deliberately lost a bet just
so you could cop a feel.

50
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Then you picked a game
you didn’t stand a chance of winning.

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Hey, shut up!

52
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
You surrendered
before your fight even got started!

53
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
[Tonpa] I... give up!

54
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Sure, I threw in the towel.
I can admit that.

55
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
But, I only wasted a couple of seconds.

56
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
-[Leorio grumbles]
-[Tonpa] You didn’t just lose.

57
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
You squandered 50 hours
we could really use right now.

58
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The least you could do
is take responsibility.

59
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
And besides,

60
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
who ever heard of a Hunter
who sucked at gambling?

61
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Shut up!

62
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
You don’t even want to become a Hunter!

63
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
The only reason you’re here
is to ruin our chances!

64
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
[chuckles]

65
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
And now you’ll have that guilt
eating away at you

66
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
for the rest of this Phase.

67
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[clatter]

68
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Hey! What are you doing?!

69
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Oops! Sorry.

70
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
This room isn’t big enough
for skateboarding, so knock it off!

71
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
[Gon] Oh...

72
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
[snoring loudly]

73
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
[Tonpa grunts]

74
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[Kurapika] Can't sleep?

75
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Not really.

76
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Thing is, I can stay awake
two or three days at a time.

77
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,000
[Kurapika] Ten hours down, huh?

78
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[Killua]
With no windows, it’s hard to tell, but…

79
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
it’s probably morning.

80
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[Kurapika] Most likely.

81
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
[mischievous chuckling]

82
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Huh?

83
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[Killua grunts]

84
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Knock it off, you guys!

85
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
[both chuckling]

86
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Some of us are tryin’ to sleep!

87
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
[groans] Gross!

88
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[laughing loudly]

89
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[chuckling]

90
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Not funny!
What the hell is wrong with you guys?

91
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
-[snores]
-You bastard!

92
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
You’d better not just be pretending
to be asleep.

93
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Damn it! Well, I guess I’m awake now.

94
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[grunts] And we’ve still got 40 more hours
left to go.

95
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
[snoring]

96
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[tapping]

97
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[Killua] Hm. I thought fishing
was just putting some bait on a hook

98
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
and throwing it in the water.

99
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Uh-huh.
But you’ve also gotta think like a fish.

100
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
And that’s supposed to work?

101
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Yup!

102
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
How would a fish feel if it saw bait
dangling in front of it?

103
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Gimme!

104
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Huh?

105
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Oh, wow!

106
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Let me give it a try!

107
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[concentrating exhale]

108
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
So, like this?

109
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
[laughs] You missed.

110
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Yeah, but watch this!

111
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[Leorio grunts]

112
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Hey! What the hell
do you think you’re doing?!

113
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Stop!

114
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
-Right on target!
-Nice!

115
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Wait! You’re gonna tear my pants!
Knock it off!

116
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
-Ya see? I landed a big one.
-Yep.

117
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Do I look like a fish to you?!
Come on! Grow up!

118
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Well, you don’t have to get so mad.

119
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
It‘s not like I’m gonna grill you
and eat you.

120
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Just leave me the hell alone!

121
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Can’t a guy just take a nap around here?

122
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
[chuckling]

123
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[annoyed grumbling]

124
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[smirks]

125
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
[Leorio] What are you smiling about?

126
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
[Tonpa] Oh, nothing.

127
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
You’re up to something again, aren’t you?

128
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
I don’t know what you mean.

129
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
All I want

130
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
is to spend the rest of our time here
in peace and quiet.

131
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
You liar.

132
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
I don’t trust you
as far as I could throw ya, got it?

133
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
[derisive snort] Feeling’s mutual.

134
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[swoosh]

135
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
[chomping quickly]

136
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
All right! Goal!

137
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Hm?

138
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
[announcer] Pokkle, applicant number 53,

139
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
and Goz, applicant number 371,

140
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
arrived simultaneously.

141
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Time elapsed, 30 hours and four minutes.

142
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Damn.

143
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Tough luck. A tie goes to

144
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,000
whichever applicant
has the lower number, old man.

145
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[derisive snort]

146
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
[Goz]
These guys must be quite skilled indeed.

147
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Hope I get a chance to fight them.

148
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
[lightly snoring]

149
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
[loud yawn]

150
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[beep]

151
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
[footsteps]

152
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
[Tonpa] You didn’t just lose.

153
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
You squandered 50 hours
we could really use right now.

154
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
The least you could do
is take responsibility.

155
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
[music plays]

156
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[grunt]

157
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[laughing]

158
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[grunting quietly]

159
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
[grunting quietly]

160
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
[grunting]

161
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[both grunting]

162
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
-[Killua laughs]
-[Gon groans]

163
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[grunts] That hurt!

164
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
[yawns]

165
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
One more hour.

166
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
[sighs]

167
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[chatters quietly]

168
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[announcer] Sommy, applicant number 118
is the thirteenth to pass.

169
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:54,000
-[chatters quietly]
-Time elapsed 61 hours and 54 minutes.

170
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
We’ve still got ten hours left?

171
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Man, I really should’ve taken more time.

172
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
[straining]

173
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Okay!

174
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I’m ready to go!

175
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
[Kurapika] One more minute…

176
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
[Leorio sighs]

177
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
This one minute’s taking forever, huh?

178
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
[buzzer goes off]

179
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Wait for us, Gon!

180
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[Gon chuckles]

181
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:35,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

182
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
BORED

183
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:44,000
[panting]

184
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Thirty minutes of running
and right we’re back where we started.

185
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Didn’t I tell you
we should’ve taken the stairs down?

186
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
[yells] This is the route
we all agreed upon,

187
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
so why don’t you shut the hell up?!

188
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
[all yelling]

189
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
[screaming]

190
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[screaming]

191
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[coughing]

192
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Killua] Man, I’m all covered in dust.

193
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Damn. Only an hour left.

194
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
If we don’t hurry, we’ll never make it.

195
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
DOOR, O - OPEN, X - CLOSE

196
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
[Leorio] We’re supposed to vote
on whether to open the door?

197
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:32,000
We need to move on,
so the choice is pretty clear.

198
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
[short beeps]

199
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
[grumbles]

200
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
I’ve had enough of your crap!

201
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
What are you talking about?
I pressed ‘O’, too!

202
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Don't lie to me!

203
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Sabotaging our chances
is your freakin’ specialty!

204
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
-Sorry, Leorio.
-Huh?

205
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
I accidentally pressed the wrong button.

206
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
What?

207
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[sighs]

208
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
-Fine, I see how it is.
-[Tonpa] Hold on.

209
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Hm?

210
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
I think you owe me an apology.

211
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
You think I’m just gonna let that slide?

212
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Maybe if you weren’t
always doing shady stuff,

213
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
this kinda thing wouldn’t happen.

214
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
I don’t owe you a thing.

215
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Almost sounds like you’re trying to say

216
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:16,000
I’m the one to blame
for everything that’s gone wrong.

217
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,000
What’s that?

218
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Don’t tell me. Have you already forgotten

219
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,000
who it was who cost us those 50 hours?

220
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
If memory serves,
I’m pretty sure that honor goes to you.

221
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
[Leorio grumbles]

222
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
-Leorio, calm down.
-[Leorio] Shut up, Kurapika!

223
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
C’mon, guys! Knock it off!

224
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
I’m the one who pressed the wrong button,
so it’s my fault!

225
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
This is stupid.

226
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
I’m going on ahead.

227
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Killua, don’t go!

228
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Hey, Gon! We must be getting real close
to the end!

229
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Whoa! Really?

230
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
[Killua] Let’s see.

231
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
“This will be the last decision
made by majority rule.

232
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Are you ready?

233
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Choose ‘O’ or ‘X’.”

234
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
And that’s it.

235
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[Leorio] Am I ready?

236
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Of course, I am! Let’s do this!

237
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
-Bastard!
-Let it go!

238
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
We don’t have time to argue.

239
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[signal beeping]

240
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[announcer] Please select a path.

241
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
There are two available options
to choose from.

242
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
The long and difficult path
which the entire group can take,

243
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
or the short and easy path

244
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
which will be limited
to only three of you.

245
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Incidentally, if you choose
the long and difficult path,

246
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
it will require a minimum
of 45 hours to complete.

247
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
while the short and easy path

248
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
will lead you directly to the goal
in approximately three minutes.

249
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Press ‘O’ to select
the long and difficult path,

250
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
or press ‘X’
to choose the short and easy path.

251
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
If ‘X’ is selected

252
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,000
two applicants from your group
must be chained to the wall with handcuffs

253
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
before the door will open.

254
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Those applicants will be unable to move
until the time limit has expired.

255
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
[Killua]
The Examiners thought of everything.

256
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Look around.

257
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Every weapon I’ve ever heard of
is down here.

258
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
So, two out of five, huh?

259
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Then they must expect us to fight
to decide which three pass.

260
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Leorio] All right.

261
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
I want to make this clear.

262
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I’m pressing the ‘X’ button.

263
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
But I’m not staying behind.

264
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
I’m one of the three that’s moving on

265
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
and I’ll do whatever it takes.

266
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
[Tonpa] You’re one to talk.

267
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:39,000
We coulda taken the long path
if you hadn’t wasted 50 hours.

268
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Why don’t you do the right thing
and make up for it by staying behind?

269
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
What’s that?!

270
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
I’m sure we all agree.

271
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
What about it, guys? Did I lie?

272
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[Gon] Hold on a second!

273
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
I’m going to press ‘O’.

274
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
It’s just we all made it this far
by working together.

275
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
We should finish together.

276
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Gon…

277
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
[Gon] It’s a big risk. I know that.

278
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
But still, we’ve got to try!

279
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Oh, come on!
It’s not a question of being a risk.

280
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
We’ve got less than an hour.

281
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,000
[exhales defiantly]

282
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Gon. There’s only one way to pass.

283
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
I mean, it’s obvious.

284
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Well, there you have it, kid.

285
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
So, now we have to pick
which three advance.

286
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
If it was up to me,

287
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
you and I are two of ‘em, Gon.

288
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,000
[smirks]

289
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Well, I’ve made it this far.

290
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
No way I’m stopping now.

291
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Whoever makes the first move wins.

292
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Is this really what it’s come to?

293
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
We have to fight amongst ourselves?

294
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
[Tonpa yelling]

295
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
That was a cheap shot!

296
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:57,000
In a fight, there’s no such thing
as a cheap shot!

297
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
[Leorio screaming]

298
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Bastard!

299
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Stop it! Both of you!

300
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Yeah! Come on! Let’s all do this together!

301
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,000
We don’t have to start fighting
until we choose ‘O’ or ‘X’, you idiot!

302
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
It’s too late for that!

303
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Then I guess
I’ll just have to choose for you!

304
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Well, two can play at that game!

305
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Looks like fighting is our only option.

306
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[Kurapika] What do we do?

307
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
[announcer] Three minutes remain.

308
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
It’s finally over, huh?

309
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Yeah. Feels like it took forever.

310
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Huh?

311
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
[tired panting]

312
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
I...

313
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,000
I...

314
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
made...

315
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
it.

316
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
[Imori] He's dead.

317
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
[Umori] Damn, what a moron.

318
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
It's better to survive
and try again next year

319
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
than to pass and die tryin’.

320
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[announcer] One minute remains.

321
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
That’s it, then.

322
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Looks like it’s just the 19 of us
that are already here.

323
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,000
[muffled rumble]

324
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Hm...

325
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Hm?

326
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:40,000
[announcer] Kurapika, number 404,
is the twentieth to pass.

327
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Killua, number 99,
is the twenty-first to pass.

328
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Gon, number 405,
is the twenty-second to pass.

329
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,000
Time elapsed 71 hours and 59 minutes.

330
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Boy, my butt hurts!

331
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I certainly wasn’t expecting
the short and easy path to be a slide.

332
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
[Hisoka] Three of them, eh?

333
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[announcer] Thirty seconds remain.

334
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Even with that big slide,
that was really close!

335
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
My hands are covered in blisters.

336
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
[Leorio] Same here.

337
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
[grunting]

338
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:16,000
[announcer] Leorio, number 403,
is the twenty-third to pass.

339
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Tonpa, number 16,
is the twenty-fourth to pass.

340
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Time elapsed 71 hours and 59 minutes.

341
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[Leorio] My hands are wrecked

342
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
but all five of us
cleared the tower together, didn’t we?

343
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
And it’s all thanks to Gon!

344
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
[grunting]

345
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
[Kurapika]
We entered the long and difficult path,

346
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,000
broke down the wall

347
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:59,000
and from there,
we snuck into the short and easy one.

348
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
I can’t believe it.

349
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
You came up with that plan on the spot!

350
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
I figured we could use those weapons

351
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
to break through the walls.

352
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
But it did take
almost all the time we had left.

353
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:15,000
[Kurapika] Even under pressure,
you were able to calmly assess our options

354
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
and think of a way to get around them.

355
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:21,000
And that is what makes you so special.

356
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,000
[buzzer rings]

357
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
[announcer] The Third Phase
of the Hunter Exam is over!

358
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,000
Twenty-five applicants have passed,

359
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
including one deceased.

360
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[narrator]
Although they had their differences,

361
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Gon found a way to bring them all together
and complete the trial as a team.

362
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
But today’s friend may be tomorrow’s foe.

363
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
What Gon doesn’t know is that before long,

364
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:54,000
they will be forced to face each other
in savage individual battles.

365
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[theme song playing]

366
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time: "Letter x From x Gon!"

367
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Mito] Always gone!

368
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[Gon] Who, me?
